	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keywords: ctl (SP 800-53 Rev 5) and 171 (SP 800-171 R2 + R3)

ctl
Query by ID (ac-2, AC-02(01), ia-2.1) or words (multi-factor).
Reverse lookups: a CSF 2.0 ID (pr.aa-05, or pr.aa for the category) or a CIS safeguard (cis 6.3, or cis 6) lists the mapped 800-53 controls.
Subtitle: baselines (L/M/H = Low/Moderate/High, P = Privacy), then the first mapped 800-171 R3 requirement, CSF subcategory and CIS safeguard (+N = more).
↩  copy ID + title + statement
⌘↩ open control on NIST CPRT
⌥↩ copy discussion (guidance)
⌃↩ copy full crosswalk (800-171 R3, R2 via R3, CSF 2.0, CIS v8.1 if installed)
⌘L large type statement + crosswalk

171
Query by ID (3.1.1, 03.01.01, 3.1, 03.01) or words. Both revisions show; CMMC Level 2 uses R2.
Subtitle: 800-53 source controls. R3 sources are NIST's (OSCAL). R2 has no official 800-53 Rev 5 mapping: it shows the sources of the same-numbered R3 requirement, labelled "via R3". Where that R3 requirement was withdrawn, it follows NIST's incorporated-into / addressed-by link (3.12.4 -&gt; 03.15.02).
↩  copy ID + title + statement
⌘↩ open requirement on NIST CPRT
⌥↩ copy 800-53 source list

Data: controls.json ships with the workflow (NIST public data). Rebuild after a NIST release: /usr/bin/python3 build_index.py

CIS v8.1 is optional and local only. Its licence (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) does not allow redistribution, so it is not included. Download "CIS Controls v8.1 Mapping to NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5" from cisecurity.org yourself, enter its path in Configure Workflow (CIS xlsx path), then run /usr/bin/python3 build_index.py in the workflow folder. The build writes cis.json next to controls.json; never share that file. Without it, cis lookups say "not indexed".

Icons: a monogram of the SP 800-53 family (800-171 requirements use their 800-53 family, so Access Control looks the same in ctl and 171); grey = withdrawn. CSF headers show the function (GV ID PR DE RS RC), CIS headers show CIS.
Regenerate icons/ after a colour change: /usr/bin/python3 -B make_icons.py
Tests: /usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest test_ctl test_sp171 test_build_index</string>
